<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
   What leaves this device, and what does not.

   A journal of things you wish you had done differently is not like other app
   data: every row is a private admission in the user's own words. Android's cloud
   backup uploads an app's whole data directory to Google by default, which would
   quietly contradict this app's "local-first, no backend" promise — and the user
   never chose it, a default did. These rules replace that default with a decision.

   Policy:

     excluded from cloud backup
       undo.db (+ its WAL sidecars)  the notes themselves
       undo_draft.xml                the half-written note currently in the composer

     still backed up
       undo_settings.xml             reminder time and theme; not sensitive
       com_revenuecat_*.xml          the anonymous app user ID and transaction
                                     metadata. Not personal content, and keeping it
                                     is what lets a paid entitlement survive a
                                     restore instead of stranding the purchase.

   Device transfer is left wide open on purpose: a direct phone-to-phone move is
   not a copy on anyone's server, so the journal travels with the user to their
   next phone. That is the balance — nothing is uploaded, and nothing is stranded.

   The consequence is real and is stated rather than hidden: lose the phone without
   having exported, and the notes are gone. Which is exactly why export and import
   are free features rather than Premium ones (see the Data section of Settings) —
   the portable file is the backup, and it is one the user holds.
-->
<data-extraction-rules>
    <cloud-backup>
        <exclude domain="database" path="undo.db" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="undo.db-wal" />
        <exclude domain="database" path="undo.db-shm" />
        <!-- Not used in WAL mode, but named so switching journal mode later cannot
             silently start uploading the journal. -->
        <exclude domain="database" path="undo.db-journal" />
        <exclude domain="sharedpref" path="undo_draft.xml" />
    </cloud-backup>
    <!-- Intentionally empty: no excludes means a device transfer carries everything. -->
    <device-transfer>
        <!-- Nothing excluded. -->
    </device-transfer>
</data-extraction-rules>
